# SauceDemo Stockton Test Automation

This repository contains automated UI tests for the SauceDemo website. The framework is built using **Playwright**, **TypeScript**, and **Gherkin** for Behavior-Driven Development (BDD).

## Prerequisites

Before running the tests locally, ensure you have the following installed:
*   [Node.js](https://nodejs.org) (v18 or higher recommended)
*   [Git](https://git-scm.com)

---

## Getting Started

### 1. Clone the Repository
Clone the repository to your local machine using Git:
```bash
git clone https://github.com
cd SauceDemo-Stockton
```

### 2. Install Dependencies
Install the required package dependencies defined in `package.json`:
```bash
npm install
```

### 3. Install Playwright Browsers
Download and configure the necessary browser binaries (Chromium, Firefox, WebKit):
```bash
npx playwright install
```

---

## Running Tests

### Generate BDD Tests
Since this project utilizes Gherkin feature files, generate the corresponding Playwright test files first if your setup requires a manual compilation step:
```bash
npx bddgen
```

### Run All Tests
Execute the entire test suite locally in headless mode:
```bash
npx playwright test
```

### Run Tests in Headed Mode
To watch the browser actions visually during test execution:
```bash
npx playwright test --headed
```

### Run a Specific Feature or Test File
```bash
npx playwright test tests/path/to/specific.spec.ts
```

### Run Scripts from the package.json
Using the short hands you can run "npm run debug" which will create the nessesary javascript files and then run any test tagged with @debug
```bash
npm run debug
npm run save
npm run report
npm run e2e
```

---

## Viewing Test Reports

After the tests complete, Playwright automatically generates an HTML report. You can open and inspect it by running:
```bash
npx playwright show-report
```